title: Game Over.
new-page: true
go-to: eg_menu
on-arrival: {!
Q.game_over = 1;
this.achieve('game_completed');
if (Q.result_type == 1) {
    this.achieve('iron_lady');
    if (Q.con_majority >= 100) {
        this.achieve('landslide');
    }
    if (Q.wet_dissent < 15 && Q.dry_dissent < 15) {
        this.achieve('one_nation');
    }
    if (Q.devolution_stance == 1) {
        this.achieve('home_rule_tory');
    }
}
if (Q.result_type == 5) {
    this.achieve('sunny_jim');
}
if (Q.autumn_election_1978 && Q.result_type >= 1 && Q.result_type <= 4) {
    this.achieve('waiting_at_the_church');
}
!}

= The End of the Beginning

@eg_menu

- #endings
- @end_game: End game.

@landslide
title: A landslide.
view-if: result_type = 1 and con_majority >= 100
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

With a majority of [+ con_majority +], you have a mandate few post-war Prime Ministers have enjoyed. On the steps of Downing Street you quote St Francis of Assisi: "Where there is discord, may we bring harmony."

The wets will stay in the Cabinet for now. They won't be able to stop you.

@working_majority
title: A working majority.
view-if: result_type = 1 and con_majority >= 20 and con_majority < 100
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

A majority of [+ con_majority +]: enough to govern, and enough to take on the unions, the money supply and the nationalised industries, if the party holds together. On the steps of Downing Street you quote St Francis of Assisi: "Where there is discord, may we bring harmony."

@slim_majority
title: A slender majority.
view-if: result_type = 1 and con_majority < 20
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

A majority of [+ con_majority +]. It is a victory, but by-elections and rebellions will eat into it, and every controversial vote will depend on the whips. The radical programme may have to wait.

@unionist_government
title: A government sustained by the Ulster Unionists.
view-if: result_type = 2
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

You are Prime Minister, kept in office by the votes of the Ulster Unionists. Their price is more Westminster seats for Northern Ireland and a firm line on security, and they will remind you of it often.

@liberal_arrangement
title: A Lib-Con arrangement.
view-if: result_type = 3
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

You enter Downing Street with David Steel's Liberals promising support vote by vote. A Speaker's Conference on electoral reform will meet within the year, and half your party already regrets it.

@minority_government
title: A minority government.
view-if: result_type = 4
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

You form a minority government and dare the opposition parties to unite against you. Like Harold Wilson in February 1974, you will probably need a second election within months to secure a majority.

@defeat
title: Defeat.
view-if: result_type = 5
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

[? if lab_mps >= 318 : James Callaghan has won a majority of his own. ?][? if lab_mps < 318 : Callaghan carries on, at the head of the largest party in a hung parliament. ?] The 1970s consensus has survived another election.

By the weekend, the Sunday papers are full of leadership speculation. Edward Heath lets it be known that he is available.

@to_be_continued
title: What comes next.
view-if: result_type >= 1 and result_type <= 4
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

This version of the game ends at the first general election. The years in government, with the 1980 Budget, the miners and the Falklands, are not written yet.

@achievements
title: Achievements
view-if: achievement_game_completed == 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu if started == 1; root.start_menu_2 if started == 0

= Achievements in this playthrough

[? if game_achievement_iron_lady : **The Iron Lady** - win a Conservative majority. ?]

[? if game_achievement_landslide : **Landslide** - win a majority of 100 or more. ?]

[? if game_achievement_one_nation : **One Nation** - win a majority with both the wets and the dries content. ?]

[? if game_achievement_no_confidence : **311 to 310** - bring down the government on a motion of no confidence. ?]

[? if game_achievement_labour_isnt_working : **Labour Isn't Working** - run the poster. ?]

[? if game_achievement_crisis_what_crisis : **Crisis? What Crisis?** - live through the Winter of Discontent. ?]

[? if game_achievement_debate_win : **The Great Debate** - win a televised debate against Callaghan. ?]

[? if game_achievement_ilford_north : **Ilford North** - win the Ilford North by-election. ?]

[? if game_achievement_ulster_deal : **Ulster Says Yes** - govern with Unionist support. ?]

[? if game_achievement_lib_con : **Lib-Con** - govern with Liberal support. ?]

[? if game_achievement_home_rule_tory : **Home Rule Tory** - win a majority after backing a Scottish Assembly. ?]

[? if game_achievement_waiting_at_the_church : **Waiting at the Church** - win Callaghan's autumn 1978 election. ?]

[? if game_achievement_sunny_jim : **Sunny Jim** - lose to Callaghan. ?]

